      "text_result": "I've diagnosed and fixed the CI failure.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause (bucket c \u2014 flawed prior solution):** The `~254` unit-test failures all shared one link/load error:\n\n```\nundefined symbol: _ZTVN5mongo18RateLimitParameterE   (vtable for mongo::RateLimitParameter)\nmold: error: libmongod_options.so: --no-allow-shlib-undefined: undefined symbol: vtable for mongo::RateLimitParameter\n```\n\nThe earlier **review-fix** (commit `2b00dfed8aa`) removed `ratelimit_parameter.cpp` from the `mongod_options` srcs list but left its matched `:ratelimit_parameter_gen` behind. The Percona IDL (`ratelimit_parameter.idl`) declares a custom `cpp_class: RateLimitParameter` with `override_set: true`; the generated code instantiates that class, but the virtual methods (the vtable) are defined only in `ratelimit_parameter.cpp`. Splitting the pair left `libmongod_options.so` with an undefined vtable, aborting every test that loads it.\n\n**Fix:** Created a dedicated `ratelimit_parameter` `mongo_cc_library` holding the matched `.cpp` + `:ratelimit_parameter_gen` pair (dep `:server_base`), removed the orphaned `:ratelimit_parameter_gen` from `mongod_options` srcs, and added `:ratelimit_parameter` to `mongod_options` deps. This restores the vtable definition and keeps the `profilingRateLimit` server parameter registered, while still honoring the reviewer's request that `ratelimit_parameter.cpp` no longer be a direct source of `mongod_options`.\n\nI confirmed via a repo-wide search (`ratelimit_parameter`, `RateLimitParameter`, `profilingRateLimit`) that these files are referenced only in `src/mongo/db/BUILD.bazel`, so this is the complete class of breakage \u2014 no other call sites needed updating.",
